package components

templ Tutorial() {
	<div class="flex gap-4 w-full h-[calc(100vh-60px)] p-4 box-border">
		// Main Tutorial Content Panel
		<div class="flex-1 bg-brand-dark text-brand-light border border-[#444444] rounded-md p-6 overflow-y-auto space-y-6 box-border leading-relaxed">
			// Header & Intro
			<div class="border-b border-[#444444] pb-4">
				<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Interactive Translation Tutorial</h1>
				<p class="text-sm text-brand-light/80">
					Learn how to translate foreign documents step-by-step using the dual-pane Desk workspace and your personal Dictionary.
				</p>
			</div>

			// STEP 1
			<section class="space-y-3">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
					<span class="bg-blue-600 text-white text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">STEP 1</span>
					Open the Tutorial Document
				</h2>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-1.5 text-sm pl-2">
					<li>Open the <strong class="text-white">Desk</strong> tab in a separate browser tab or window.</li>
					<li>In the search bar at the top, type <code class="bg-[#262626] border border-[#383838] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-blue-300">Tutorial</code>.</li>
					<li>Click on the document titled <strong>Tutorial</strong> to load it into your workspace.</li>
				</ol>
			</section>

			// STEP 2
			<section class="space-y-3">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
					<span class="bg-blue-600 text-white text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">STEP 2</span>
					Compare the Dual Panes
				</h2>
				<div class="bg-[#262626] border border-[#383838] rounded-lg p-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
					<p>
						Once loaded, you will see a chat conversation between <strong class="text-gray-200">Alex</strong> and <strong class="text-gray-200">Sam</strong>:
					</p>
					<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs font-mono">
						<div class="bg-[#1e1e1e] border border-[#333333] p-3 rounded">
							<span class="text-blue-400 font-bold block mb-1">Left Pane (Original Source)</span>
							<p class="text-gray-300">&quot;Hello! My name is Alex. I am new here...&quot;</p>
						</div>
						<div class="bg-[#1e1e1e] border border-[#333333] p-3 rounded">
							<span class="text-yellow-400 font-bold block mb-1">Right Pane (Your Translation)</span>
							<p class="text-yellow-200/80">[unknown]! [unknown] [unknown] [unknown] [unknown]...</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p class="text-xs text-brand-light/70">
						Every word displayed as <code class="text-yellow-300 font-mono">[unknown]</code> means it has not been saved in your personal dictionary yet.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			// LANGUAGE & TRANSLATION SEMANTICS
			<section class="space-y-3">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
					<span class="bg-purple-600 text-white text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">SEMANTICS</span>
					Understanding Language &amp; Token Semantics
				</h2>
				<div class="bg-[#262626] border border-[#383838] rounded-lg p-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
					<p class="text-brand-light/90">
						Before adding entries to your dictionary, keep in mind how meaning and word structure are evaluated across languages and conlangs:
					</p>
					<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
						<div class="bg-[#1e1e1e] border border-[#333333] p-3 rounded space-y-1">
							<span class="text-purple-300 font-semibold block">1. Lexical Meaning vs. Context</span>
							<p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
								A single word often carries multiple nuances depending on context (polysemy). Choose a concise core definition—or include a brief gloss like <code class="text-purple-200">&quot;be (3rd sg.)&quot;</code> { "for" } <code class="text-gray-200">is</code>—so the meaning stays clear across different sentences.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="bg-[#1e1e1e] border border-[#333333] p-3 rounded space-y-1">
							<span class="text-purple-300 font-semibold block">2. Shared Roots, Suffixes &amp; Morphology</span>
							<p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
								Some words share a common root or stem but attach different suffixes to mark tense, plurality, or grammatical role (such as <code class="text-gray-200">greet</code> vs. <code class="text-gray-200">greeting</code>, or <code class="text-gray-200">name</code> vs. <code class="text-gray-200">names</code>). Because dictionary lookups match exact surface forms, each root-and-suffix variation—alongside irregular forms like <code class="text-gray-200">am</code> and <code class="text-gray-200">is</code>—is stored as its own separate token.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="bg-[#1e1e1e] border border-[#333333] p-3 rounded space-y-1">
							<span class="text-purple-300 font-semibold block">3. Idioms &amp; Non-Literal Phrases</span>
							<p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
								Fixed social expressions like <em>&quot;nice to meet you&quot;</em> rarely map 1-to-1 across languages or conlangs. Focus on capturing the semantic intent of each component word rather than forcing rigid literal equivalents.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="bg-[#1e1e1e] border border-[#333333] p-3 rounded space-y-1">
							<span class="text-purple-300 font-semibold block">4. Punctuation &amp; Token Boundaries</span>
							<p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
								Surrounding punctuation (<code class="text-gray-200">!</code>, <code class="text-gray-200">?</code>, <code class="text-gray-200">.</code>) is preserved in the layout while the core word token is matched—so <code class="text-gray-200">Hello!</code> resolves directly to your entry { "for" } <code class="text-gray-200">hello</code>.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			// STEP 3
			<section class="space-y-3">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
					<span class="bg-blue-600 text-white text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">STEP 3</span>
					Add Your First Translation Entry
				</h2>
				<div class="space-y-2 text-sm pl-2">
					<p>Let us translate Alex&apos;s first word, <strong class="text-white">&quot;Hello&quot;</strong>:</p>
					<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-1.5 text-sm">
						<li>Click on the word <code class="bg-[#262626] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-gray-200 font-mono">Hello</code> in the left pane (or open your <strong>Dictionary</strong> tab).</li>
						<li>Enter the target translation { "for" } <code class="bg-[#262626] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-gray-200 font-mono">Hello</code> (e.g., your translated term).</li>
						<li>Click <strong class="text-white">Save / Add to Dictionary</strong>.</li>
					</ol>
				</div>
			</section>

			// STEP 4
			<section class="space-y-3">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
					<span class="bg-blue-600 text-white text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">STEP 4</span>
					Observe Live HTMX Updates
				</h2>
				<div class="bg-[#262626] border border-[#383838] rounded-lg p-4 space-y-2 text-sm">
					<p>
						As soon as you save <strong class="text-white">&quot;Hello&quot;</strong>, the Desk automatically re-renders the right pane:
					</p>
					<div class="bg-[#1e1e1e] border border-[#333333] p-3 rounded text-xs font-mono">
						<span class="text-green-400 font-bold block mb-1">Updated Right Pane</span>
						<p class="text-gray-200">
							<span class="text-green-400 font-bold">[Your Translation]</span>! [unknown] [unknown] [unknown] [unknown]...
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			// STEP 5
			<section class="space-y-3">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
					<span class="bg-blue-600 text-white text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">STEP 5</span>
					Complete the Dialogue
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm pl-2">
					Continue adding the remaining words to your dictionary line-by-line until all chat bubbles are fully translated:
				</p>

				<div class="bg-[#262626] border border-[#383838] rounded p-4 text-xs space-y-3">
					<div>
						<strong class="text-blue-400 block mb-1">Line 1 (Alex):</strong>
						<span class="text-gray-300">&quot;Hello! My name is Alex. I am new here. What is your name?&quot;</span>
					</div>
					<div>
						<strong class="text-blue-400 block mb-1">Line 2 (Sam):</strong>
						<span class="text-gray-300">&quot;Hi Alex! My name is Sam. Welcome! It is nice to meet you.&quot;</span>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="bg-green-950/40 border border-green-700/50 rounded p-3 text-xs text-green-200/90 flex gap-2 items-center">
					<span>🎉</span>
					<span>
						Once every word is saved, no <code class="font-mono text-yellow-300">[unknown]</code> placeholders will remain, completing your document translation!
					</span>
				</div>
			</section>

			// Further Assistance Footer
			<div class="border-t border-[#444444] pt-4">
				<div class="bg-[#262626] border border-[#383838] rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-3 text-sm">
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-white font-semibold">Need Further Assistance?</h3>
						<p class="text-xs text-brand-light/80 mt-0.5">
							Visit the <a href="/community" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">Community</a> forums to ask questions or check out the <a href="/help" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">Help</a> page for further assistance.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="flex items-center gap-2 shrink-0 text-xs">
						<a href="/community" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded bg-[#1e1e1e] hover:bg-[#333333] text-gray-200 border border-[#383838] transition-colors">
							Community
						</a>
						<a href="/help" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-500 text-white font-medium transition-colors">
							Help Page
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		// Sidebar Chat
		@SideBar([]templ.Component{Chat()})
	</div>
}